 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 667119,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The function <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">np.multiply(arr1, arr2)</code> receives two <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">ndarray</code> objects <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">arr1</code> and <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">arr2</code> with the same dimensions, and performs element-wise multiplication. What is the output of the following code?\n<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">import numpy as np\n\narr1 = np.array([[1, 2], [3, 4]])\narr2 = np.array([[1, 0], [0, 1]])\nout = np.multiply(arr1, arr2)\nprint(out)\n</pre>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1330318,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">[[1 0]\n[0 4]]\n</pre>",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "The result of element-wise multiplication between <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">arr1</code> and <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">arr2</code> is:\n<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">\n[[1 0]\n[0 4]]\n</pre>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1330319,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">[[1 2]\n[3 4]]\n</pre>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">np.multiply()</code> performs element-wise multiplication and not a matrix multiplication between the two arrays. What is the result of performing the element-wise multiplication on <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">arr1</code> and <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">arr2</code> objects?"
    },
    {
     "id": 1330320,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">[[2 2]\n[3 5]]</pre>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">np.multiply()</code> multiplies two arrays of the same size element-wise. What is the result of performing the element-wise multiplication on <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">arr1</code> and <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">arr2</code> objects?"
    }
   ],
